"hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2761,"Abu Bakr (RA) said in the narration of Jabir (RA) which I have mentioned before:
*""Until his two feet sank into the valley's depths, he ran until he ascended, then he walked.""*

**CHAPTER:**"
2762,"Narrated to us Bishr ibn Mu'adh: narrated to us Ayyub (meaning Ibn Waqid): narrated to us 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:
""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would run (sa'ya) in the valley of the Masil between Safa and Marwah.""

**CHAPTER:**"
2763,"Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj al-Razi, that 'Amr ibn Mujammi' informed them, on the authority of Musa ibn 'Uqba, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:
""When the mount of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood still for him at Dhu al-Hulayfa during the Farewell Pilgrimage or an 'Umra, he would say the Talbiya (Labbayk Allahumma labbayk).""
Then he mentioned the hadith and said:
""Then he came to al-Safa, and he ran between al-Safa and al-Marwa seven times. When he passed by al-Mas'a, he would run.""

**CHAPTER:**"
